assassin's creed valhalla is getting a  whole second year of post-launch content  kicking off with the crossover stories  dlc that sees odyssey's cassandra and  valhalla's avor meet but the first major  expansion for year two is dawn of  ragnarok in which aver witnesses javi's  adventures during the earliest days of  one of the most well-known moments of  norse myth and the following video we go  over everything that we learned about  dawn of ragnarok during a preview event  if you enjoyed the video be sure to  leave a like and subscribe to the  channel dawn of ragnarok takes place  after the events of the asgard and  jotunheim sagas so if you haven't gotten  that far in assassin's creed valhalla  and don't want to be spoiled this is  your final warning to pause this video  and come back later don't worry we'll  still be here  the asgard and yotenheim sagas conclude  with javi aka odin learning that there's  no way for them to physically survive  ragnarok however they can undergo an  experimental procedure to be born again  that's where assassin's creed sages come  from they're isu from javi's time that  go on to be reborn as humans knowing  that they and their allies will be  reborn following ragnarok javi faces the  coming end of the world dawn of ragnarok  picks up there with hobby seeking out  their son balder who has been kidnapped  and imprisoned within the realm of the  dwarves a land that has been consumed by  war ahead of ragnarok javi's quest will  see them once again face the frost  giants of jotunheim but they'll go up  against a more fiery foe too certa we  still don't know what abort's  motivations are in dawn of ragnarok only  that they turned to velka to relive  these memories of javi after having  vivid nightmares of baldur presumably  javi has a message for aver embedded in  their memories but we'll just have to  wait and see if donna ragnarok is  anything like odyssey's myth-based  expansion the fate of atlantis then avor  could be in store for a major  ramification or two donna ragnarok is  coming from ubisoft sophia the lead  studio for assassin's creed iii  liberation assassin's creed rogue and  assassin's creed origins the curse of  the pharaohs dlc  giles armstrong is senior scriptwriter  for donna ragnarok his other work  includes being the lead writer on  destruction all-stars and a writer for  marvel's guardians of the galaxy ubisoft  sophia told gamespot via email that  donna ragnarok takes inspiration from  the poetic edda and many of the norse  sagas the studio describes the entire  expansion as a 35 plus hour experience  which takes place on a map that's about  one-third the size of valhalla's england  though the expansion takes place after  the events of the asgard and yotenheim  sagas you'll be able to jump into dawn  of ragnarok even if you haven't  completed those storylines and although  you might be a little lost as to what's  going on ubisoft sophia told gamespot  that it has taken special care to make  sure that new players will be just as  engaged with the narrative as those who  have completed valhalla  [Music]  as seen in the cinematic trailer for  dawn of ragnarok javi will possess new  elemental and supernatural powers in  this expansion they will have the power  to command both ice and fire as well as  shape-shift regarding these new powers  ubisoft sophia told gamespot quote the  new powers add a new aspect to the  combat but not only they will alter the  way players explore the world sneak  around solve puzzles and also fight the  armies of muspelheim are dangerous and  deadly being creatures of fire players  will quickly find themselves needing an  edge over them sometimes they might need  to mitigate some of the incoming damage  and use the power of muspelheim to  temporarily become immune to lava and  flame in other situations players will  need to be on the offensive and quickly  shut down the enemy in all cases though  players should be on the lookout for  changing the powers acquired in the  hygge rip as the battleground evolves  end quote the hugo rip is the main new  gameplay mechanic in dawn of ragnarok as  its name suggests it allows you to rip  away and acquire the powers and  abilities of others it can only store up  to two abilities at once though so  you'll have to be strategic and how you  craft hobbies build some abilities are  aimed at stealth while others are more  combat or navigation focused when  designing this new mechanic ubisoft  sophia told gamespot that had two goals  for the hygge rip to provide players the  agency to play how they wanted and to  embrace the fantasy of playing as a god  who gains power by stealing it from  their enemies ubisoft sophia wrote quote  we wanted to really make a difference in  all players gameplay no matter if they  like face-to-face combat stealthily  taking out the opposition exploring the  realm of the dwarves in search of the  dwarves ancient secrets and mystery or  solving puzzles to get the valuable  treasure the powers will let odin reach  inaccessible locations give them new  stealth opportunities let them traverse  the world in a different manner and lay  devastation on the forces of jotunheim  and mussolheim activating the powers  costs hooger and old norse the term  roughly means the spirit the mind and  thoughts of living beings or their life  force all living things carry it and  odin can refill it by defeating enemies  animals draining it from hoogar blooms  or even sacrificing some of their own  life for hygge at shrines of yggdrasil  end quote beyond the abilities already  mentioned javi will also be able to  imbue their weapons with freezing  effects and raise defeated enemies from  the grave as allies if the cinematic  trailer is any indication javi will be  able to teleport to arrows they fired as  well outside of the story dawn of  ragnarok will include plenty of optional  content too such as a battle arena  that's run by a valkyrie where you can  take on different kinds of combat trials  if you're wondering how javi's gender is  handled in dawn of ragnarok it's  basically the same as it was in valhalla  in a statement to gamespot ubisoft  sophia said quote in dawn of ragnarok  players will experience a continuation  of avor story the rules under which the  animus operates remain the same and  players will be free to decide whether  they want to play with a female or male  character or ultimately let the animus  choose the stronger memory stream end  quote we also asked ubisoft montreal  lead developer for assassin's creed  valhalla why the latest mainline game is  getting so many post-launch expansions  as opposed to immediate sequels rather  the druids and siege of paris are both  each 7 to 10 hours long and dawn of  ragnarok clocks in at 35 hours you could  argue all three are expansive enough to  be combined as a whole new game that's a  follow-up to avor story in valhalla  ubisoft montreal could have gone for an  assassin's creed brotherhood or  revelations approach but chose not to in  response ubisoft montreal emailed back  to say quote to be honest it's a  question that we asked ourselves as well  for the team in general this felt like  the most cohesive way to give this  offering to the players the team has  made efforts to have all content be more  accessible to players expansions  included so they can explore the world  of valhalla not unlike a theme park we  wanted players to be able to choose  which saga they embarked on be it in  england ireland franchia and now the  realm of the dwarves expansions one and  two focused more on the viking facets of  valhalla and exploring avor as a  character under different situations now  dawn of ragnarok feels like the other  side of the coin where we go deeper into  the norse mythology and more so into  odin harvey's backstory and what we have  focused on giving players the ability to  play all the content in the order they  see fit we also felt it was important to  still have these offerings connected one  experience is complementary to the other  given how important norse mythology was  to viking everyday life we felt dawn of  ragnarok needed to be included in  assassin's creed valhalla end quote don  of ragnarok is scheduled to release as  paid dlc on march 10th be sure to  subscribe to gamespot to stay informed  on assassin's creed and be notified when  we post previews like this one if open  world games like assassin's creed are  your thing and you're wondering how 2022  is going to shape up you can check out  our preview for first spoken right now  but before you leave let us know in the  comments where you think valhalla should  go next in its second year of post  launch content do you think ubisoft is  going to stick to javi for the rest of  2022 or will we see a war story get some  further development as well  you
 

